From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shipwright <shipwright@invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:47:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prefer a powered Bluetooth adapter and allow pinning one

Upstream 7f16e3c ("Add dynamic Bluetooth adapter detection") already
enumerates adapters with GetManagedObjects, starts without an adapter and
picks one up when BlueZ adds it. It selects the lowest object path,
though, whether or not that adapter is powered, and offers no way to
choose. On a machine where hci0 exists but is down and hci1 is the
working controller, the daemon binds to the dead one.

- Track each adapter's Powered state as reported by GetManagedObjects
  and InterfacesAdded, and prefer a powered adapter at startup.
- Follow every adapter's Powered state afterwards, through one match
  rule for org.bluez.Adapter1 PropertiesChanged under /org/bluez.
- When the selected adapter is unpowered and a powered adapter appears,
  or another known adapter is powered on, switch to it.
- Read the selected adapter's properties with one GetAll.
- On removal of the selected adapter, prefer a powered replacement.
- MAGICPODS_ADAPTER=hci1 (or a full /org/bluez/... path) pins the
  adapter. Until the pinned adapter exists the daemon runs without one,
  as it already does when there is no adapter at all.
- Log when no usable adapter is available yet.

The environment override and powered-first policy come from the
adapter-discovery patch in SailfishOS-MagicPods by Alzareus
(https://github.com/Alzareus/SailfishOS-MagicPods, GPL-3.0), written for
the Jolla Phone (2026), which has no hci0 at all. That patch predates
upstream's DBusBtAdapter; this is a re-implementation of its policy on
top of the new class.

Based-on-patch-by: Alzareus <https://github.com/Alzareus>
